From 5e61d630f0ad67af09e528e33869485011421855 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William King <wking53214@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 10:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] F-J: converter for queue-identity mismatch between
 ingress and worker

First live run of ingress+worker together (every prior session tested
them separately) found they resolve to DIFFERENT Redis key prefixes on
stock defaults -- TRANSMISSION_NAMESPACE="tq" (ingress) vs --queue-name
"v12" -> "sq:v12" (worker). A submitted job sat at pending forever,
worker silently polled an empty keyspace, no error anywhere. Proven
live before and after the fix.

Chose a converter over a handshake: SENTINEL_QUEUE_ID is now the one
identifier both processes derive their prefix from by default, instead
of two independently-set values that happen to need to agree.
TRANSMISSION_NAMESPACE / SENTINEL_QUEUE_NAME remain as explicit
escape-hatch overrides for anyone deliberately running isolated queues.

Verified: stock-defaults job now completes in <1s; 20 concurrent calls
across 2 real workers -> 20/20 done, 14 ledger rows matching 14
governed calls sent; test_queue_identity_converter.py (4 tests) locks
in the fix and the negative case (explicit mismatched overrides still
correctly fail, since those remain intentionally independent knobs).

Full suite 100/100 (67 baseline + 29 breaker/rate-limiter + 4 new),
three clean runs, each suite its own process.
